-- title:
--   Graded quotient data defines a point of the Hilbert functor
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $n, m$, a commutative ring $A$ and a function $h : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ with $h(d) = \binom{n+d}{n}$ for all $d < m$. Suppose given, for every $d$, an $A$-module $N_d$ and an $A$-linear map $\Theta_d$ from the submodule of degree-$d$ homogeneous polynomials in $A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ to $N_d$, such that for every $d \ge m$: $N_d$ is a finite $A$-module, $N_d$ is a projective $A$-module, the rank of $N_d$ at the stalk at every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $A$ equals $h(d)$, $\Theta_d$ is surjective, and the kernels are stable under multiplication by forms, i.e. if $F$ is homogeneous of degree $d$ with $\Theta_d(F) = 0$ and $G$ is homogeneous of degree $e$, then $\Theta_{e+d}(GF) = 0$. The conclusion is that there is a term $p$ of type `Point A n h`, that is, an ideal $p.I$ of $A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ closed under taking homogeneous components, whose degree-$d$ graded piece — the quotient of the degree-$d$ forms by those lying in $p.I$ — is, for every $d$, a finite projective $A$-module of rank $h(d)$ at every prime of $A$, and such that $p.I$ is the ideal generated by all forms $F$ of some degree $d \ge m$ with $\Theta_d(F) = 0$.
--
--   This is the packaging step which converts a system of surjections from the graded pieces of $A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ onto finite projective modules of prescribed rank, with multiplicatively closed kernels, into a point of the Hilbert functor of $\mathbb{P}^n$ with Hilbert function $h$ over $A$. It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.exists_point_I_eq_span_of_isClosedImmersion_of_flat_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.exists_point_I_eq_span_of_isClosedImmersion_of_flat_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation), where the data $(N_d, \Theta_d)$ arise from a flat closed subscheme of $\mathbb{P}^n_A$.
